<div style="font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Inter',Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;color:#1F1F1C;line-height:1.5"><h1 style="font-size:22px;font-weight:600;margin:0 0 4px">Shreyas / Maya 1:1</h1><p data-role="meta" style="color:#65655F;margin:0 0 16px">Wednesday, October 7, 2026 at 09:01 · 18 min</p><h2 style="font-size:16px;font-weight:600;margin:20px 0 8px">Attendees</h2><p>Shreyas, Maya Chen</p><h2 style="font-size:16px;font-weight:600;margin:20px 0 8px">Notes</h2><h4>Decisions</h4><ul><li>Maya comes off the on-call rotation for the next two weeks, starting 7 October and returning on 21 October, with Shreyas as primary and Diego as secondary for sync.</li><li>Maya takes Friday 9 October off.</li><li>Maya is paused from phone screens until the end of the month but will do final-round interviews for the senior backend role.</li><li>No contractor for the Microsoft side of Calendar Sync v2; hiring energy goes into the senior backend hire instead.</li><li>Calendar Sync v2 dates hold (beta 13 November, GA 4 December); a Google-only beta is a fallback to revisit in two weeks, not the plan.</li><li>The Microsoft subscription renewal design adds an hourly reconciliation sweep for unhealthy subscriptions and an alert when more than one percent of subscriptions are expired.</li><li>The recurring-event test harness (moved occurrences, cancelled occurrences, series time zone changes) is part of Calendar Sync v2 scope.</li><li>For customer-impacting incidents, Tom owns customer updates, Shreyas owns internal updates with an hourly cadence, and the person fixing it only talks in the incident channel.</li></ul><h4>Key facts</h4><ul><li><strong>When does Calendar Sync v2 go to beta?</strong> 13 November 2026, with GA on 4 December 2026.</li><li><strong>What is the main risk on the Microsoft side of Calendar Sync v2?</strong> Microsoft Graph webhook subscriptions for calendar events expire after roughly three days, so each technician&#39;s subscription must be renewed or Deino silently stops receiving that person&#39;s changes.</li><li><strong>How will subscriptions be kept alive?</strong> A renewal job every six hours that renews anything expiring in the next 24 hours, a handler for Microsoft lifecycle notifications, and a reconciliation sweep with delta queries (daily for everyone, hourly for unhealthy subscriptions).</li><li><strong>When does Maya go back on call?</strong> On 21 October 2026, after two weeks off the rotation.</li><li><strong>Why did Shreyas not want a contractor?</strong> Ramp-up time would run past the beta, any contractor with production access is in SOC 2 scope once the observation window opens on 1 November, and a Graph contractor costs fifteen to twenty thousand dollars a month when the senior backend role is already approved.</li><li><strong>How many phone screens had Maya done recently?</strong> Four in the last two weeks.</li><li><strong>When would Maya&#39;s staff promotion take effect?</strong> Realistically 1 January 2027, the start of the next quarter, after Aisha reviews Shreyas&#39;s promo doc.</li><li><strong>What does Shreyas think Maya should grow in for staff?</strong> Writing for people outside engineering, for example writing the next customer-facing postmortem.</li><li><strong>What key does Calendar Sync now use to identify events?</strong> The iCalUID plus the recurrence ID, for both Google and Microsoft.</li><li><strong>How will Calendar Sync v2 cut over from polling for beta customers?</strong> Five-minute polling keeps running alongside push; disagreements are logged and polling is trusted, and once the disagreement rate is near zero for a week polling drops to hourly as a safety net.</li><li><strong>What did Shreyas tell Maya about the board meeting?</strong> The board approved both hires (senior backend and mobile), Deino is not raising now, Series A conversations start in March, and runway is about nineteen months.</li><li><strong>How much of the daily Google API quota does polling use?</strong> About forty percent with five-minute polling; push should bring it under ten percent.</li></ul><h2 style="font-size:16px;font-weight:600;margin:20px 0 8px">Action items</h2><ul style="list-style:none;padding-left:4px"><li>☑ Update the PagerDuty on-call schedule to take Maya off for two weeks and post it in the eng channel <span data-role="meta" style="color:#65655F">— Shreyas, due Oct 7, 2026</span></li><li>☐ Tell the recruiter to take Maya off the screening rotation <span data-role="meta" style="color:#65655F">— Shreyas, due Oct 7, 2026</span></li><li>☐ Send Maya the Fernhollow postmortem draft for a technical check <span data-role="meta" style="color:#65655F">— Shreyas, due Oct 8, 2026</span></li><li>☐ Finish the subscription renewal section of the Calendar Sync v2 design doc and send it to Shreyas and Priya <span data-role="meta" style="color:#65655F">— Maya Chen, due Oct 12, 2026</span></li><li>☐ Talk to Aisha about prioritising the senior backend hire over the mobile hire <span data-role="meta" style="color:#65655F">— Shreyas, due Oct 8, 2026</span></li><li>☐ Write Maya&#39;s staff-engineer promotion doc <span data-role="meta" style="color:#65655F">— Shreyas, due Oct 16, 2026</span></li><li>☐ Send Shreyas a list of the things she is proudest of from this year <span data-role="meta" style="color:#65655F">— Maya Chen, due Oct 12, 2026</span></li><li>☐ Write the incident communication rules (owners, hourly updates, single channel) into the incident runbook <span data-role="meta" style="color:#65655F">— Shreyas, due Oct 21, 2026</span></li></ul><h2 style="font-size:16px;font-weight:600;margin:20px 0 8px">Insights</h2><h3 style="font-size:14px;font-weight:600;margin:12px 0 4px">Decisions</h3><ul><li>Maya comes off the on-call rotation for the next two weeks, starting 7 October and returning on 21 October, with Shreyas as primary and Diego as secondary for sync. <span data-role="meta" style="color:#65655F">— Shreyas, 00:01</span></li><li>Maya takes Friday 9 October off.</li><li>Maya is paused from phone screens until the end of the month but will do final-round interviews for the senior backend role.</li><li>No contractor for the Microsoft side of Calendar Sync v2; hiring energy goes into the senior backend hire instead.</li><li>Calendar Sync v2 dates hold (beta 13 November, GA 4 December); a Google-only beta is a fallback to revisit in two weeks, not the plan.</li><li>The Microsoft subscription renewal design adds an hourly reconciliation sweep for unhealthy subscriptions and an alert when more than one percent of subscriptions are expired.</li><li>The recurring-event test harness (moved occurrences, cancelled occurrences, series time zone changes) is part of Calendar Sync v2 scope.</li><li>For customer-impacting incidents, Tom owns customer updates, Shreyas owns internal updates with an hourly cadence, and the person fixing it only talks in the incident channel.</li></ul></div>
